{
  "id": "ss.fx.thornbed",
  "name": "Thornbed",
  "description": "The ground a vine leaves when it withers, and the one thing in this weapon that outlives the plant. Drawn as ground rather than as a wash: three discs falling off in alpha instead of one hard circle, so the patch has no rim and never reads as a painted lid laid over the floor \u2014 which is what the tinted disc it replaces always looked like. The runners cross the patch rather than radiating from its middle, because a set of stems all pointing at one centre is a star and this is a plant that fell over where it stood; the thorns stand out of them at uneven heights and lean every way, for the same reason. `$timber.dark` for dead wood and `$husk` for the barbs, which is the same pairing the weapon's own vine uses, so a player who has watched one come up reads this without being told what it is. The pivot is the document's centre and `meta.radius` is the patch's own reach, so the game scales it by the ground the find actually denies.",
